    "Values": "Values",
    "0 dBm corresponds to exactly 1 mW; P_mW must be positive. dBm values can be added and subtracted like decibels when combining losses and gains along a link.": "0 dBm corresponds to exactly 1 mW; P_mW must be positive. dBm values can be added and subtracted like decibels when combining losses and gains along a link.",
    "A high BCF flags substances (e.g. many lipophilic organics) that accumulate strongly in tissue relative to water. Assumes steady-state uptake from water only, ignoring dietary exposure routes.": "A high BCF flags substances (e.g. many lipophilic organics) that accumulate strongly in tissue relative to water. Assumes steady-state uptake from water only, ignoring dietary exposure routes.",
    "A is often used to look up standard spiral tables. A larger A gives a gentler, more gradual transition; A equals the radius at the point where the spiral's radius of curvature equals its own length.": "A is often used to look up standard spiral tables. A larger A gives a gentler, more gradual transition; A equals the radius at the point where the spiral's radius of curvature equals its own length.",
    "A larger K-value means a flatter, more gradual vertical curve; K is commonly checked against minimum sight-distance requirements.": "A larger K-value means a flatter, more gradual vertical curve; K is commonly checked against minimum sight-distance requirements.",
    "A lower centre of gravity and wider track both reduce load transfer, improving cornering grip balance. Treats the vehicle as a rigid body and ignores suspension roll and weight distribution front-to-rear.": "A lower centre of gravity and wider track both reduce load transfer, improving cornering grip balance. Treats the vehicle as a rigid body and ignores suspension roll and weight distribution front-to-rear.",
    "A power factor of 1 means all supplied power does real work; lower values indicate more reactive power relative to real power. P and S must be in consistent units (W and VA).": "A power factor of 1 means all supplied power does real work; lower values indicate more reactive power relative to real power. P and S must be in consistent units (W and VA).",
    "A value of 0 means every site has the same species composition; larger values indicate greater turnover between sites. Gamma should be at least as large as alpha since it pools all sites.": "A value of 0 means every site has the same species composition; larger values indicate greater turnover between sites. Gamma should be at least as large as alpha since it pools all sites.",
    "APC plus the average propensity to save equals 1. APC can exceed 1 when consumption is financed by borrowing or by drawing down savings, which is common at low income levels.": "APC plus the average propensity to save equals 1. APC can exceed 1 when consumption is financed by borrowing or by drawing down savings, which is common at low income levels.",
    "Absorption rate constant": "Absorption rate constant",
    "Accelerometer Tilt Angle (Single-Axis)": "Accelerometer Tilt Angle (Single-Axis)",
