    "All disks are assumed to have equal capacity d; a RAID 0 array offers no fault tolerance, so any single disk failure loses all data. The result uses the same capacity unit as d.": "All disks are assumed to have equal capacity d; a RAID 0 array offers no fault tolerance, so any single disk failure loses all data. The result uses the same capacity unit as d.",
    "All masses should be entered in atomic mass units (u). A larger mass defect means a more tightly bound, more stable nucleus.": "All masses should be entered in atomic mass units (u). A larger mass defect means a more tightly bound, more stable nucleus.",
    "Angle a": "Angle a",
    "Angle b": "Angle b",
    "Angle off heading/target direction": "Angle off heading/target direction",
    "Angular velocity omega must be in rad/s, not rpm. This library also has RPM-based torque-power formulas elsewhere that include the 2·pi/60 conversion factor; use this SI/direct form only when omega is already in rad/s.": "Angular velocity omega must be in rad/s, not rpm. This library also has RPM-based torque-power formulas elsewhere that include the 2·pi/60 conversion factor; use this SI/direct form only when omega is already in rad/s.",
    "Annual operating expenses": "Annual operating expenses",
