    "BML governs a ship's resistance to trim (pitching); it is normally much larger than the transverse metacentric radius BM. Assumes small-angle trim and a rigid, unflooded hull.": "BML governs a ship's resistance to trim (pitching); it is normally much larger than the transverse metacentric radius BM. Assumes small-angle trim and a rigid, unflooded hull.",
