    "Defines Poisson's ratio directly as the negative ratio of lateral strain to axial strain, nu = -(strain_lat/strain_ax), for a material under uniaxial load. It quantifies how much a material contracts sideways as it stretches lengthwise.": "Defines Poisson's ratio directly as the negative ratio of lateral strain to axial strain, nu = -(strain_lat/strain_ax), for a material under uniaxial load. It quantifies how much a material contracts sideways as it stretches lengthwise.",
    "Defines the shear modulus directly as the ratio of shear stress to shear strain, G = tau_s/gamma, within the elastic range of a material. It measures a material's resistance to shape-changing (shearing) deformation.": "Defines the shear modulus directly as the ratio of shear stress to shear strain, G = tau_s/gamma, within the elastic range of a material. It measures a material's resistance to shape-changing (shearing) deformation.",
    "Density and both velocities must be in SI units for a result in pascals. Assumes an isotropic elastic medium; Vp must sufficiently exceed Vs for a physically meaningful positive bulk modulus.": "Density and both velocities must be in SI units for a result in pascals. Assumes an isotropic elastic medium; Vp must sufficiently exceed Vs for a physically meaningful positive bulk modulus.",
    "Density and velocity must be in SI units (kg/m^3 and m/s) so the result comes out in pascals. Assumes an isotropic, elastic medium, as is standard in seismic velocity analysis.": "Density and velocity must be in SI units (kg/m^3 and m/s) so the result comes out in pascals. Assumes an isotropic, elastic medium, as is standard in seismic velocity analysis.",
