    "Divides a gas's molar mass by the average molar mass of air (about 28.8 g/mol) to give its vapor density relative to air. Values above 1 mean the vapor is denser than air and tends to sink and pool.": "Divides a gas's molar mass by the average molar mass of air (about 28.8 g/mol) to give its vapor density relative to air. Values above 1 mean the vapor is denser than air and tends to sink and pool.",
    "Divides the break-even sales level by actual sales and multiplies by 100 to show what percentage of current sales is needed just to cover costs. A lower ratio indicates a larger safety margin above break-even.": "Divides the break-even sales level by actual sales and multiplies by 100 to show what percentage of current sales is needed just to cover costs. A lower ratio indicates a larger safety margin above break-even.",
    "Divides the density of a substance by the density of a reference liquid (usually water) to give specific gravity, a dimensionless ratio comparing the two densities.": "Divides the density of a substance by the density of a reference liquid (usually water) to give specific gravity, a dimensionless ratio comparing the two densities.",
    "Divides trip distance by fuel economy to get fuel used, then multiplies by the price per unit of fuel, giving the total fuel cost of the trip.": "Divides trip distance by fuel economy to get fuel used, then multiplies by the price per unit of fuel, giving the total fuel cost of the trip.",
    "Divides waist circumference by hip circumference to give the waist-to-hip ratio, a standard measure of body fat distribution used to assess health risk.": "Divides waist circumference by hip circumference to give the waist-to-hip ratio, a standard measure of body fat distribution used to assess health risk.",
