    "Solves the valence-weighted neutralization relation Ca·Va·na = Cb·Vb·nb for the base volume Vb needed to exactly neutralize a given acid, as (Ca·Va·na)/(Cb·nb). Valence is the number of acidic or basic equivalents per formula unit (1 for HCl, 2 for H2SO4, etc.).": "Solves the valence-weighted neutralization relation Ca·Va·na = Cb·Vb·nb for the base volume Vb needed to exactly neutralize a given acid, as (Ca·Va·na)/(Cb·nb). Valence is the number of acidic or basic equivalents per formula unit (1 for HCl, 2 for H2SO4, etc.).",
