    "Use consistent SI units (m² for As, Pa for fy and f'c, m for d and b) to get Mn in newton-metres. Assumes a singly reinforced, tension-controlled section per ACI-style Whitney block assumptions; does not check reinforcement ratio limits.": "Use consistent SI units (m² for As, Pa for fy and f'c, m for d and b) to get Mn in newton-metres. Assumes a singly reinforced, tension-controlled section per ACI-style Whitney block assumptions; does not check reinforcement ratio limits.",
    "Use the absolute permeability mu (H/m), not a relative value; for free space enter 1.2566e-6, and for a magnetic core use mu0 times the material's relative permeability. Field strength H is in amperes per metre.": "Use the absolute permeability mu (H/m), not a relative value; for free space enter 1.2566e-6, and for a magnetic core use mu0 times the material's relative permeability. Field strength H is in amperes per metre.",
    "Use thrust (giving TSFC, thrust-specific fuel consumption) for jet and turbofan engines, or shaft power (giving PSFC) for turboprop and piston engines; keep the output unit consistent with the quantity chosen. Lower values indicate a more fuel-efficient engine.": "Use thrust (giving TSFC, thrust-specific fuel consumption) for jet and turbofan engines, or shaft power (giving PSFC) for turboprop and piston engines; keep the output unit consistent with the quantity chosen. Lower values indicate a more fuel-efficient engine.",
    "Used in hazardous-materials safety assessment to judge whether a vapor will accumulate near the ground; assumes ideal-gas behavior and dry air composition.": "Used in hazardous-materials safety assessment to judge whether a vapor will accumulate near the ground; assumes ideal-gas behavior and dry air composition.",
    "Uses the US customary tablespoon (3 teaspoons); UK/metric tablespoons are sometimes rounded to 15 mL exactly, which differs slightly.": "Uses the US customary tablespoon (3 teaspoons); UK/metric tablespoons are sometimes rounded to 15 mL exactly, which differs slightly.",
    "Uses the US customary teaspoon; UK/metric teaspoons are sometimes rounded to 5 mL exactly, which differs slightly.": "Uses the US customary teaspoon; UK/metric teaspoons are sometimes rounded to 5 mL exactly, which differs slightly.",
    "Uses the avoirdupois pound and ounce, the common units for everyday weight; troy ounces used for precious metals are different.": "Uses the avoirdupois pound and ounce, the common units for everyday weight; troy ounces used for precious metals are different.",
    "Valid only when I is greater than I_threshold; the model is linear and ignores rollover (thermal saturation) at high current. Slope efficiency eta_slope is in watts of optical output per ampere of drive current.": "Valid only when I is greater than I_threshold; the model is linear and ignores rollover (thermal saturation) at high current. Slope efficiency eta_slope is in watts of optical output per ampere of drive current.",
    "Valid only while the sensor is stationary or moving at constant velocity, since any dynamic acceleration adds error. ax must not exceed g in magnitude, or the arcsine is undefined.": "Valid only while the sensor is stationary or moving at constant velocity, since any dynamic acceleration adds error. ax must not exceed g in magnitude, or the arcsine is undefined.",
