    "All heats of formation must be standard values measured under the same reference conditions (typically 25°C, 1 atm), with coefficients from a correctly balanced equation. This simplified form supports up to two reactants and two products; reactions with more species require summing additional terms externally.": "All heats of formation must be standard values measured under the same reference conditions (typically 25°C, 1 atm), with coefficients from a correctly balanced equation. This simplified form supports up to two reactants and two products; reactions with more species require summing additional terms externally.",
