    "Estimates mean arterial pressure (MAP) as the product of cardiac output (CO) and total peripheral resistance (TPR), analogous to Ohm's law (V = I×R) applied to the circulatory system. This relationship underlies how changes in cardiac output or vascular resistance affect blood pressure.": "Estimates mean arterial pressure (MAP) as the product of cardiac output (CO) and total peripheral resistance (TPR), analogous to Ohm's law (V = I×R) applied to the circulatory system. This relationship underlies how changes in cardiac output or vascular resistance affect blood pressure.",
    "Estimates the broad-sense heritability (H²) of a trait using Falconer's formula, which doubles the difference in concordance rates between monozygotic (MZ) and dizygotic (DZ) twins. Because MZ twins share ~100% of their genes and DZ twins share ~50% on average, doubling the gap isolates the genetic contribution to trait variance.": "Estimates the broad-sense heritability (H²) of a trait using Falconer's formula, which doubles the difference in concordance rates between monozygotic (MZ) and dizygotic (DZ) twins. Because MZ twins share ~100% of their genes and DZ twins share ~50% on average, doubling the gap isolates the genetic contribution to trait variance.",
    "Estimates the enthalpy change of a gas-phase reaction using average bond dissociation energies, by taking the energy required to break the bonds in the reactants minus the energy released forming the bonds in the products.": "Estimates the enthalpy change of a gas-phase reaction using average bond dissociation energies, by taking the energy required to break the bonds in the reactants minus the energy released forming the bonds in the products.",
    "Estimates the mass percent of oxygen in an organic compound by subtracting the measured carbon and hydrogen mass percentages from 100%, assuming the sample contains only carbon, hydrogen, and oxygen.": "Estimates the mass percent of oxygen in an organic compound by subtracting the measured carbon and hydrogen mass percentages from 100%, assuming the sample contains only carbon, hydrogen, and oxygen.",
    "Estimates the molar solubility of an AB-type sparingly soluble salt in the presence of a common ion, given the solubility product Ksp and the concentration of the common ion already present in solution.": "Estimates the molar solubility of an AB-type sparingly soluble salt in the presence of a common ion, given the solubility product Ksp and the concentration of the common ion already present in solution.",
    "Estimates the recombination frequency between two linked genes from a test-cross or F2 offspring count, expressed as the percentage of recombinant offspring among the total. This value is used to construct genetic linkage maps, where 1% recombination frequency corresponds to 1 map unit (centimorgan).": "Estimates the recombination frequency between two linked genes from a test-cross or F2 offspring count, expressed as the percentage of recombinant offspring among the total. This value is used to construct genetic linkage maps, where 1% recombination frequency corresponds to 1 map unit (centimorgan).",
    "Estimates the time since two lineages diverged from a common ancestor using the molecular clock hypothesis. It divides the observed proportion of sequence differences between the two lineages by twice the substitution rate, since substitutions accumulate independently along both branches since divergence.": "Estimates the time since two lineages diverged from a common ancestor using the molecular clock hypothesis. It divides the observed proportion of sequence differences between the two lineages by twice the substitution rate, since substitutions accumulate independently along both branches since divergence.",
