    "Requires P(B) > 0; both pab and pb must lie within the valid probability range [0, 1], and pab cannot exceed pb.": "Requires P(B) > 0; both pab and pb must lie within the valid probability range [0, 1], and pab cannot exceed pb.",
    "Requires a > 0 and |x| ≤ a (equivalently |x/a| ≤ 1) for the result to be real-valued.": "Requires a > 0 and |x| ≤ a (equivalently |x/a| ≤ 1) for the result to be real-valued.",
    "Requires a > 0 and |x| ≤ a for real-valued results; this antiderivative underlies the derivation of the area of a circle via ∫√(a²−x²)dx.": "Requires a > 0 and |x| ≤ a for real-valued results; this antiderivative underlies the derivation of the area of a circle via ∫√(a²−x²)dx.",
    "Requires a > 0; a should be the semi-major axis (a ≥ b) for the result to correspond to the standard ellipse latus rectum.": "Requires a > 0; a should be the semi-major axis (a ≥ b) for the result to correspond to the standard ellipse latus rectum.",
    "Requires a > 0; the eccentricity of a hyperbola is always greater than 1, unlike an ellipse whose eccentricity lies between 0 and 1.": "Requires a > 0; the eccentricity of a hyperbola is always greater than 1, unlike an ellipse whose eccentricity lies between 0 and 1.",
    "Requires a > b > 0; if a ≤ b the result does not correspond to a valid focal distance and the roles of the two axes should be swapped.": "Requires a > b > 0; if a ≤ b the result does not correspond to a valid focal distance and the roles of the two axes should be swapped.",
    "Requires a ≠ 0. To obtain a definite integral, evaluate this expression at the upper and lower bounds and subtract the results.": "Requires a ≠ 0. To obtain a definite integral, evaluate this expression at the upper and lower bounds and subtract the results.",
    "Requires a ≠ 0; the logarithmic term is well-defined for all real x since x + √(x²+a²) is always positive.": "Requires a ≠ 0; the logarithmic term is well-defined for all real x since x + √(x²+a²) is always positive.",
    "Requires complete combustion with all carbon converted to CO2 (no soot or CO formation) and an accurately known sample mass; uses the molar mass ratio C/CO2 = 12/44.": "Requires complete combustion with all carbon converted to CO2 (no soot or CO formation) and an accurately known sample mass; uses the molar mass ratio C/CO2 = 12/44.",
    "Requires complete combustion with all hydrogen converted to H2O and an accurately known sample mass; uses the molar mass ratio 2H/H2O = 2/18. Any moisture in the sample or absorption tube must be excluded from the measured water mass.": "Requires complete combustion with all hydrogen converted to H2O and an accurately known sample mass; uses the molar mass ratio 2H/H2O = 2/18. Any moisture in the sample or absorption tube must be excluded from the measured water mass.",
    "Requires p ≠ 1; when p = 1 the sequence is arithmetic and this formula is undefined (division by zero). The formula assumes n ≥ 1 with a1 as the first term.": "Requires p ≠ 1; when p = 1 the sequence is arithmetic and this formula is undefined (division by zero). The formula assumes n ≥ 1 with a1 as the first term.",
    "Requires r ≠ 1, since the closed-form derivation divides by (1−r)². When r = 1 the sum simplifies to n(n+1)/2 and must be computed separately.": "Requires r ≠ 1, since the closed-form derivation divides by (1−r)². When r = 1 the sum simplifies to n(n+1)/2 and must be computed separately.",
    "Requires vector b to be nonzero (x2 and y2 not both zero); the result is the scalar magnitude along b, not the full vector projection.": "Requires vector b to be nonzero (x2 and y2 not both zero); the result is the scalar magnitude along b, not the full vector projection.",
