    "The Weber fraction is only approximately constant within a mid-range of stimulus intensities; it tends to break down at very low or very high intensities near the absolute threshold or saturation.": "The Weber fraction is only approximately constant within a mid-range of stimulus intensities; it tends to break down at very low or very high intensities near the absolute threshold or saturation.",
    "The axis of revolution must not intersect the curve, and r must be the distance from the curve's centroid to the axis.": "The axis of revolution must not intersect the curve, and r must be the distance from the curve's centroid to the axis.",
    "The axis of revolution must not intersect the region, and r must be the distance from the region's centroid to the axis, not from an edge of the region.": "The axis of revolution must not intersect the region, and r must be the distance from the region's centroid to the axis, not from an edge of the region.",
    "The coefficient 61.5 (≈ 2.303·RT/F) assumes a temperature of about 37°C (mammalian body temperature); for experiments at room temperature (~20°C), the standard coefficient is closer to 58 and would need to be adjusted accordingly.": "The coefficient 61.5 (≈ 2.303·RT/F) assumes a temperature of about 37°C (mammalian body temperature); for experiments at room temperature (~20°C), the standard coefficient is closer to 58 and would need to be adjusted accordingly.",
    "The direction vector (dx, dy, dz) must be nonzero; all coordinates should be expressed in the same length unit for the distance to be meaningful.": "The direction vector (dx, dy, dz) must be nonzero; all coordinates should be expressed in the same length unit for the distance to be meaningful.",
    "The result should be rounded to the nearest integer in practice, since n must be a whole number; a value far from an integer suggests an error in the empirical formula or the measured molar mass.": "The result should be rounded to the nearest integer in practice, since n must be a whole number; a value far from an integer suggests an error in the empirical formula or the measured molar mass.",
    "The two vectors represent adjacent sides of the triangle from the shared vertex; if the vectors are parallel (collinear), the computed area is zero.": "The two vectors represent adjacent sides of the triangle from the shared vertex; if the vectors are parallel (collinear), the computed area is zero.",
    "Theta must be given in radians; convert degrees to radians (theta × π/180) before use. Positive theta rotates the point counterclockwise.": "Theta must be given in radians; convert degrees to radians (theta × π/180) before use. Positive theta rotates the point counterclockwise.",
    "This simplified two-age-class version assumes discrete, non-overlapping reproductive events at ages 1 and 2 and constant survivorship/fecundity values across individuals; real life tables often include more age classes.": "This simplified two-age-class version assumes discrete, non-overlapping reproductive events at ages 1 and 2 and constant survivorship/fecundity values across individuals; real life tables often include more age classes.",
